-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Version 0.2.0 (2026-11-08)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  * Dismiss on every problem notice, beside Repair (ORDER 468; Daniel, 2026-11-08: "a dismiss on the problems of the
    computer so the person can choose to not see it anymore, along side a config page with all the dismissed and
    current ones"): the notifier's Hide is now Dismiss, the summary at login has Dismiss all, and a dismissal is told
    once, with where the problem stays listed and Open Problems. A dismissal made on the page closes the notification
    at once; a problem brought back there is told again
  * The Problems page in System Settings (System Administration): the current problems and the dismissed ones, each
    with its title, text, since when, severity, Repair where there is one, the record's own actions, Dismiss, and
    Bring back for a dismissed one; it follows the stores (a problem that appears or ends is listed or goes at once);
    an empty state in plain words. A failed service that fails the same way again at a later boot stays dismissed
    (sparky-stereo-problems 0.2.0)
  * Strings in the nine required languages

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Version 0.1.0 (2026-11-02)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  * First release (ORDER 350): the session's side of sparky-stereo-problems, one notifier for every package of
    the edition. At login one notification per open problem, or one summary when several are open; then one for
    each new or changed problem; a failed problem is Critical and stays, a degraded one or a notice is Normal
  * Each problem offers Show details (its evidence: the command, its exit status, its output, the repair and the
    last repair), Repair (through pkexec for the machine's and this boot's problems), the record's own actions and
    Hide, which is the person's and comes back when the problem changes or a repair fails
  * One notifyrc (sparky-stereo-problems.notifyrc), so System Settings' Notifications page lists every event;
    the strings in the nine required languages
